CommitDate: Fri Oct 2 07:21:07 2026 -0500

    fix: short-text keyword threshold for title-mode consult. Addresses LORE-043.
    
    The tick-start consult (LORE-007) classifies board-row TITLES, which are
    short: the realistic 4-word title "worker worktree checkout collision"
    carries 3/8 of the shared-checkout-collision keywords (raw score 0.375),
    below the flat 0.6 KEYWORD_THRESHOLD, so consult returned matched:false
    for the fleet's most recurring collision class (dogfood 2026-10-01
    run 4). LORE-041 fixed the title+detail path where the detail holds the
    canonical git error paste; this fix targets the TITLE-ONLY path.
    
    Shape: a length-scoped keyword GATE, not a blanket threshold drop.
    
    - lore/classifier.py: new SHORT_TEXT_WORD_LIMIT (8) and
      SHORT_KEYWORD_THRESHOLD (0.3) constants plus _keyword_gate(text), which
      picks the gate by word count; _keyword_confidence() takes the gate as a
      parameter and classify/classify_all/near_misses all pass the
      length-scoped gate so the three surfaces stay consistent. The cutoff is
      principled and measured: board census (65 rows) has title p25 = 8 words
      / median 14; the longest refusal pinned by near-miss tests ("container
      env lost the API key after .env got clobbered") is 10 words, so 9 or a
      naive 12 would flip pinned refusals — 8 keeps every existing pin.
    - Honesty rule intact: keyword confidence stays capped at 0.5 with
      keyword-only evidence, below-gate texts still return unclassified with
      the near-miss echo, the long-text 0.6 gate is unchanged, and the
      registry is untouched (13 curated classes, no new ids).
    - tests: new tests/test_lore043_short_text_threshold.py (20 cells: the
      title labels via classify/classify_all/consult/CLI; long 0.5-score and
      quarter-score refusals survive; short below-gate refuses; sibling
      classes keep their boundaries; title+detail signature path unchanged)
      plus the LORE-021 naming-contract test now compares against the same
      length-scoped gate the classifier used.
    - docs: README/INSTALL consult sections document the short-title band;
      skills/lore-usage blind-spot note updated (the run-4 gap is fixed);
      USAGE skill dev-loop count stale literal 364->404 fixed in passing;
      test-count literals synced (384->404, new canonical count);
      CHANGELOG entry.
